From 8bf08e5f9d3cf6424c11db077c8d17d1b62fe93d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] background jobs: drop the login shell's rc output
 before the command (start marker)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

spawn_local runs every background job as `$SHELL -lic '... exec bash -c "$HERMES_BG_COMMAND"'`,
so whatever the host's startup files print became the job's first output. Ubuntu's
/etc/bash.bashrc prints its sudo hint for any account without ~/.sudo_as_admin_successful
(a fresh VM, a faked HOME), and the CLI dock painted an idle job as
`⚙ sleep 30 · 0s · last: See "man sudo_root" for details.` instead of `starting`.
The readers stripped only bash's job-control warnings.

Fix: just before the `exec`, the login shell prints a per-job start marker on its own line
(`printf '\n%s\n' __hermes_bg_start_<uuid>__`; the leading newline ends an unterminated rc
line). `_ingest_output` holds everything until that line and drops it with the marker, so
poll/log/the dock/watch patterns/notify output see only the command's own output; motd,
locale and cloud-init banners go too. It covers the pipe, log (persisted/worker) and PTY
readers, since all three ingest through `_ingest_output`.

- Armed only when the argv actually carries the marker (`arm_start_gate`): Windows argv is
  unchanged and prints none, an adopted foreground Popen has none, a replaced argv has none.
- `start_marker` is checkpointed, so a re-adopted persisted job re-reading its log from the
  start is gated too; old checkpoints default to "" (ungated, as before).
- No marker by end of output (an rc file that exits, a shell that fails): the held text is
  released as is (`_finish_reader`, and the log reader's adopter path).
- Hold bounded at 64 KiB: past it, everything but a possible marker-prefix tail is released.
- notify_on_complete and watch-pattern semantics unchanged (they scan ingested text only).
- `clean_shell_noise` moved to process_registry_bg_shell (offsets process_registry.py growth).

Proof:
- RED at origin/main: tests/tools/test_process_registry_start_banner.py, 5 failed; the
  pipe/log/pty cases fail on `'To run a command as administrator ...\nno-newline-bannerfirst-line\n'
  == 'first-line\n'` (a temp rc prints Ubuntu's banner plus an unterminated line).
- GREEN: that file 7 passed; 230 test files referencing process_registry/ProcessSession/
  spawn_local: 3905 passed, 3 failed, all 3 in tests/gateway/test_persist_job_survives_gateway_restart.py
  with RestartSafeScopeUnavailable, which fails identically at origin/main on this Kanban worker.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, 10/10 killed): e.g. M1 `_ingest_output` never gates ->
  test_rc_banner_never_reaches_output_or_dock[pipe|log|pty] fail; M10 marker printed without
  its leading newline -> same three fail (the unterminated banner line swallows it); others:
  no marker in argv, armed without marker, no release in _finish_reader / log reader, no
  __post_init__ arming, marker not checkpointed, no \r tolerance (PTY), no hold bound.

Card: t_01a1d69d460bc977 (found by t_01a1d6822cd87a47; PR #2643 made the dock test hermetic).
